+# Story timing and an early dashboard
+
+Issue #181. Design candidate for the AITM dogfood workflow. The durable product design keeps Core #2, the usage monitor #100, and the viewer on their existing paths.
+
+## What can ship first
+
+| Slice | Inputs and output | Delivery gate |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| A. Capture and mine the evidence | Record normalized timing receipts on `planning` using a short operator or skill checklist. Run one read-only snapshot command over a pinned planning commit. Emit canonical JSON for mining and a read-only validation report. Seed it with the ten observations already recorded in #181. | Reproduce the board backfill and its limitations. Round only for display. Exercise manual live capture on one approved child with a scope switch, one tool interval and one owner wait. |
+| B. Local story dashboard | Render that same snapshot as one standalone HTML file. Open it locally and refresh on demand. Filter by epic, status, and coverage. Drill into a row for phase and role totals, evidence, last progress event, and the direct versus child split. | Serve from static bytes without credentials, server, production Core, or monitor cutover. The dashboard still works with timing or cost missing. |
+| C. Product integration | Swap in Core's supported pinned read view and the monitor's compatible export or report. Let the eventual viewer and hosted provider project the same measures. | The consumers reproduce the same fixture and retain provenance, coverage, and calibration exclusions. Core and the monitor deliver and qualify their own interfaces on their existing schedules. |
+
+The first dashboard is a project-local snapshot for AITM dogfooding. It gives a story list with **State**, **Last progress**, **Estimate**, **Actual** in decimal agent-hours, **Elapsed** in calendar time, **Owner wait**, **Cost** in API-equivalent USD, and explicit coverage. Show the planning commit and timestamp, and a separate usage cutoff and pricing basis when present. Use the canonical story and evidence links for drilldown. A partial value carries its qualifier in the cell. Missing data reads Unknown. An in-progress story shows age only if its start is evidenced, labeled as age rather than elapsed delivery. Read-only freshness uses a supplied as-of time and does not imply live telemetry. No live dashboard server or hosted publication is required for these slices.
+
+Existing seed evidence is enough for a useful first snapshot. #100 has 8.4586 observed agent-hours and #133 has 2.1983, both partial. #111 has 0.6074 observed agent-hours across pickup through closure. Its 12m 54s from Develop to Done is an independently bounded implementation-delivery elapsed time. The seed's Cost values are Unknown. These are historical observations through their pinned cutoff, not current live figures.
+
+## Store facts on planning now
+
+The current database is the versioned `.aitm/` planning store. Keep workflow transitions and relationships in the existing per-story events. Use one sanitized immutable receipt per source batch under `.aitm/stories/<bucket>/<story>/attachments/timing/<receipt-id>.json` for new direct story evidence. Epic receipts contain direct epic observations; child observations live with their child. A batch spanning stories is split by proven scope and published in one Git commit. Only a designated workflow recorder for each story publishes its receipts. Unresolved scope stays out of story totals. Keep draft evidence private until graduation proves a stable draft-to-story link, then publish eligible observations with original occurrence times and the link. Keep unpublished or ambiguous observations in a private pending queue; their contents do not appear in a published snapshot.
+
+Use the existing v0 backfill as an explicitly registered legacy seed at its recorded digest. Treat its interval rows as direct facts and recompute totals; the supplied inclusive totals and readback are verification targets. If a later receipt covers the same evidence, require an explicit overlap reconciliation or supersession before counting it. Preserve the original seed.
+
+A versioned dogfood receipt carries project and story or proven draft alias, phase, optional attempt, actor and role, logical turn or request pseudonym, evidence kind, coverage, basis and safe locator or digest, occurrence interval or boundary, and recorded UTC time. Use integer milliseconds and half-open intervals. Preserve occurrence and recording time separately. Stable event identities derive from the normalized source identity and scope, independent of the import run. Identical repeats are idempotent. An incompatible payload for an existing identity is held pending reconciliation. Corrections append a new receipt naming the exact prior record and revision; old pinned snapshots stay reproducible. Keep transcripts, provider handles, local paths, prompts, tool output, and credentials in private evidence. Uncertain Git publication is resolved by rereading the branch for the exact receipt bytes before retrying. The snapshot reader accepts only supported schemas and rejects an invalid or conflicting receipt for the affected measurement with a reason.
+
+The operator checklist is to bind the active story and phase before a turn, record a genuine scope change before switching, mark an explicit owner request and response or resolution, record evidenced turn and tool boundaries, and publish a sanitized batch after a verifiable checkpoint. Capture elapsed boundaries from workflow milestones. If a boundary cannot be recovered, record the gap and leave that metric Unknown or partial. A recorder can attach a fixed, sanitized existing usage export or a report receipt to the same snapshot when it proves story attribution. A manual time entry never creates a token observation. Check replay and published board values before recording any later projection. The local dashboard reads a committed snapshot and does not write to the board or mutate the planning checkout.
+
+## Shared metric contract
+
+- **Elapsed:** report two explicitly scoped clocks. All-phase delivery uses first evidenced story or draft kickoff and verified delivery completion. Implementation delivery uses the selected attempt's Develop entry and verified Done boundary. Default dashboard elapsed to all-phase when evidenced, with a labeled implementation scope available in detail. No substitution between scopes. For an epic use its own start and verified finish. Missing endpoints yield Unknown. Elapsed includes intervening waits and idle.
+- **Actual:** union qualified turn intervals per logical actor, within scope, and add different actors even if their intervals overlap. Count tool time inside the turn once. Exclude that actor's owner wait, idle, and unattended execution outside a turn. A wait for one actor does not remove another actor's work. Conflicting simultaneous attribution for one actor is unresolved until evidence supports a split. Roll up each distinct child or descendant once plus direct epic planning and orchestration. Keep dependencies outside ancestry. Preserve the optional union across actors as observed working wall time, separate from delivery elapsed and additive effort.
+- **Cost:** use attributed monitor token quantities and versioned rates, with independent usage coverage, publication cutoff and pricing basis. Keep known priced subtotals distinct from complete totals. Tool runtime never adds a charge. Unattributed or unavailable cost stays Unknown at story level. Use canonical ancestry and the monitor's direct/inclusive semantics to prevent double-counting.
+- **Calibration:** pair the fixed estimate revision with the same phase, attempt or outcome, actor and role scope, and measurement basis. All-phase board Actual cannot substitute for an implementation-only actual. Preserve partial and Unknown records for analysis and exclude them from calibration.
+
+Example fixture: child A works 09:00–10:30, child B 09:30–11:00, owner wait 11:00–11:30, direct epic work 11:30–11:45. Verified delivery at 11:45 gives 2h 45m elapsed, 2h 15m observed working wall time, and 3.25 agent-hours Actual. Cost follows the attributed requests only.
+
+## Ownership and transition
+
+Core C23/#28 owns activity admission and the qualified implementation trip clock, C25/#34 owns review timing, and C44/#51 owns versioned estimate/outcome and compatible usage ingestion. Reuse their identities, timing evidence, phase and attempt boundaries, overlap rules, and coverage. Board Actual includes in-turn tool time and never authorizes a Core trip. The dogfood receipt is an evidence intake format, not a second lifecycle or a new authority. Define an explicit, idempotent mapping to supported Core records at integration, retain source digests and coverage, and hold unsupported facts for future adapters.
+
+The monitor owns qualified provider attribution, usage, pricing, and publication. Use #100 M06–M07 and the M07b split for capture and scope contracts, M13 for the pinned project and story view, and M14 for versioned export into C44. Until those land, consume only the installed collector's supported fixed-sequence evidence where attributable; pin ledger sequence, time basis, rate version and coverage. Keep time and usage cutoffs visible and avoid claiming a common cutoff across mismatched sources. Additional providers fit the same contract when their surfaces qualify. A provider lacking trustworthy timing or pricing still contributes evidence to the measures it supports.
+
+#181 owns the dogfood intake, snapshot and display integration. The later viewer can adopt the snapshot fields and Core read interfaces. Contract changes identified in design go to the owning epic once, with dependent consumers named. No parallel schema, timing engine, token-rate engine, or board writer is added to #2 or #100 by this design.
+
+## Acceptance
+
+1. A reader pinned to the same planning commit, as-of time and usage receipt produces identical normalized rows across rebuilds. The existing ten-row seed matches the recorded board values and carries partial coverage and no Cost.
+2. Replay duplicate and conflicting records, a late correction, a draft alias and an interrupted multi-story publication. Each observation counts at most once and prior pinned views remain unchanged.
+3. Verify the parallel fixture, same-actor tool overlap, explicit owner waits, scoped elapsed endpoints, and a missing endpoint. An estimate with mismatched phase, role, or partial coverage cannot calibrate.
+4. Run a controlled dogfood capture with a provider qualified for the chosen boundaries. Verify safe receipts and a refreshed dashboard row while timing or cost from another source is absent. Verify a fresh reader can reconstruct it without a running Core service.
+5. With a fixed monitor usage fixture, compare priced totals, pricing basis and unknown coverage with the source report. Additional tool time with unchanged tokens changes Actual only. No unauthenticated provider data enters story totals.
+6. Verify the local dashboard displays direct and child contributions, all qualifiers and snapshot provenance, and escapes story text before rendering. The static artifact does not expose private evidence and works offline.
